cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this workflow, its scripts, or the bundled example scenario, please cite it as below."
title: "Alicante Centro Ciudad SUMO Traffic Scenario Generation and FCD Extraction Workflow"
type: software
version: 1.3.6
date-released: "2026-09-01"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/FUMD-AI/fumd-ai-urban-mobility-data-generation"
url: "https://github.com/FUMD-AI/fumd-ai-urban-mobility-data-generation"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible workflow for generating synthetic urban traffic demand
  scenarios on an OpenStreetMap-derived SUMO network of central Alicante,
  Spain, and for extracting Floating Car Data (FCD) - including geographic
  coordinates and traffic-signal state - from each simulated scenario.
  Covers the full chain from OpenStreetMap extraction (Overpass API,
  Geofabrik + osmium, or pyrosm) through netconvert network conversion,
  randomTrips.py/duarouter-based stochastic trip generation across four
  vehicle-count densities (900/1000/1200/1400) with three replicates each,
  and SUMO microsimulation producing per-scenario FCD trajectory files.
  Output from this workflow is intended as the raw SUMO input to the
  FUMD-AI preprocessing workflow (fumd-ai-preprocessing-workflow), which
  turns raw SUMO/OMNeT++ output into AI-ready datasets for cellular
  handover / migration prediction.
keywords:
  - SUMO
  - traffic simulation
  - floating car data
  - FCD
  - OpenStreetMap
  - netconvert
  - randomTrips
  - reproducibility
  - FAIR
  - urban mobility
